  "question": {
    "text": "The number of integer values of $m$, for which the $x$ -coordinate of the point of intersection of the lines $3 x+4 y=9$ and $y=m x+1$ is also an integer, is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "t9yTW",
      "text": "0",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "PkXp9",
      "text": "2",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "1kpL7",
      "text": "4",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Sdsby",
      "text": "1",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given lines are, $3 x+4 y=9$\r\n$$\r\ny=m x+1\r\n$$\r\nSolving Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get\r\n$$\r\nx=\\frac{5}{3+4 m}\r\n$$\r\nIf $m=-1,$ then $x=-5$ and $m=-2,$ then $x=-1$ are the only \r\npossibilities.",
    "image": null
